# SCREENPLAY · a calculator made of fish: say 6 + 4 out loud and a fish answers 10.
# The wiring table, and why each fish is there, is docs/game/worked-builds.md.
# It is an ADDING machine: it keeps the last two digits it hears and adds them, so the
# + is only a separator. Eight etched Full Adders do the arithmetic; the tens digit is
# c4 OR (s3 AND (s1 OR s2)), and the units are the sum plus six whenever that is true.

include scenes/a-calculator-board.play

# ── 6 · park the fish that answers, let the cold board settle, then ask it ──
run /freeze "Say"
run /nudge "Say" -200 200
run /nudge "Say" 6 0
run /fps 1
tick 10
snap 6 · the board settled, every coil that denies zero has said so
run 6 + 4
tick 140
expect < 10 >
snap 6 · the answer, on Say's own panel
